<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ovbel half yr attrib income slides to loss.</title>
<headline>Ovbel half yr attrib income slides to loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-abnormal	  3.7	   vs 4.0</p>
<p>    - post abnormal	 2.2 loss    vs 4.0 profit</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   0.66 loss   vs 1.19 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.06	  vs 1.74</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.30	  vs 0.29</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.01	  vs 1.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		  10.99	 vs 27.28</p>
<p>Full name: Ovebel Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	  1.76	  vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors of Ovbel, a property company, said the abnormal item was from a bad debt incurred in Pretoria and headlease losses.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
